WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.133
Task decomposition.

2
00:00:02.433 --> 00:00:07.133
The single skill that decides whether a long running agent finishes or wanders.

3
00:00:08.333 --> 00:00:14.700
Task decomposition turns a fuzzy goal, like research this and write a brief, into concrete subtasks.

4
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.633
Each subtask gets a done criterion and its dependencies.

5
00:00:18.933 --> 00:00:23.033
An agent can't tell it is making progress unless progress is checkable.

6
00:00:24.233 --> 00:00:26.300
Good subtasks have three properties.

7
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:30.400
They are verifiable: a condition your code can check, not a vibe.

8
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.394
They are dependency aware.

9
00:00:32.394 --> 00:00:36.433
Independent subtasks run in parallel, and dependent ones wait.

10
00:00:36.733 --> 00:00:40.900
And they isolate failure, so when one fails you know exactly what is missing.

11
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.733
Here is a tiny task graph.

12
00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:46.533
Fetching orbital data needs nothing else.

13
00:00:46.833 --> 00:00:50.733
Fetching news coverage also needs nothing, so it runs in parallel.

14
00:00:51.033 --> 00:00:53.779
Writing the brief needs both, so it waits.

15
00:00:53.779 --> 00:00:56.133
Each box has its own done criterion.

16
00:00:57.333 --> 00:01:00.133
Ask the model for the task list as structured data.

17
00:01:00.433 --> 00:01:04.300
The first task lists the fields that must be present, and needs nothing.

18
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:08.300
The brief cites the earlier outputs, and needs tasks one and two.

19
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:13.333
Here is a maximally fuzzy question: is Earth having a bad week?

20
00:01:13.633 --> 00:01:22.933
The agent decomposes it into three pulls, near Earth objects, solar storms, and natural disasters, plus a synthesis task needing all three.

21
00:01:23.233 --> 00:01:27.733
When the storm data fails, the task list shows exactly which box is unticked.

22
00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:32.243
So the final answer honestly says space weather data is unavailable.

23
00:01:32.243 --> 00:01:34.533
Wandering agents don't have that map.

24
00:01:35.733 --> 00:01:36.561
Let's recap.

25
00:01:36.561 --> 00:01:38.767
Break fuzzy goals into subtasks.

26
00:01:39.067 --> 00:01:41.567
Give each a verifiable done criterion.

27
00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:43.733
Track dependencies as a graph.

28
00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:46.442
Then failures stay local and visible.

29
00:01:46.442 --> 00:01:48.200
Next up: short term memory.
